Message:
fix: defense-in-depth bare-string coercion across remaining 7 nodes

Extends the EXPLAIN coercion pattern from 684e9e2 to every other LLM
node (chunk, infer, relate, activate + 3 cross-video). Llama-class
models on the shared Methodex key occasionally return bare-string lists
where dicts are expected; the codebase owner explicitly said standard
users must not hit format failures, so this is across-the-board defense.

Per-node helpers added:
- chunk._coerce_chunk_items → wraps strings into {chunk_id, text, type=quote, speaker, ...}
- infer._coerce_inference_items → wraps strings into {chunk_id, inferences=[text]}
- relate._coerce_pattern_items → wraps strings into {pattern_id, pattern_name, description, supporting_inferences, relationship_type=convergent}
- activate._coerce_principle_items → wraps strings into {principle_id, principle, source_insight, how_might_we, rationale}
- cross_relate._coerce_meta_pattern_items → wraps strings into {meta_pattern_id, pattern_name, description, source_videos, ...}
- cross_explain._coerce_cross_insight_items → wraps strings into {cross_insight_id, headline, explanation, consistency=medium, ...}
- cross_activate._coerce_system_principle_items → wraps strings into {system_principle_id, principle, context_adaptations, ...}

Each helper:
- returns non-list inputs unchanged (validator still produces its normal error)
- drops empty/whitespace-only strings
- logs `[NODE] Coerced N bare-string item(s) into dict shape` only when coercion happens
- is called twice per node (once after initial LLM call, once after the validation-failure retry)

Tests: backend/tests/test_node_coercion.py — 56 new tests (49 parameterized
helper unit tests + 7 explain_node-style integration tests with mocked
llm_service). 456 tests total (was 400). ruff clean.

